* SPICE models for the motor-driver watchdog.
*
* 2N3904 / 2N3906: the widely distributed standard models (the ones LTspice
* and most vendor libraries ship). BF is scaled per run (BFSCALE) to cover the
* hFE spread; at the 10-300 uA collector currents used here real parts sit
* well inside 0.3x..1.5x of these values.
*
* BAT85: small-signal Schottky, DO-34. Parameters approximate the NXP / Vishay
* published model (Vf ~0.22 V at 1 mA, 25 C). IS is scaled per run (ISSCALE)
* to cover the datasheet Vf spread (about +/-40 mV). A 1N5817 or BAT43 in the
* same position behaves the same at these currents.

.model Q2N3904 NPN(IS=6.734f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF={416.4*BFSCALE} NE=1.259
+ ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5 BR=.7371 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1 CJC=3.638p
+ MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=.2593 VJE=.75 TR=239.5n TF=301.2p
+ ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)

.model Q2N3906 PNP(IS=1.41f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=18.7 BF={180.7*BFSCALE} NE=1.5
+ ISE=0 IKF=80m XTB=1.5 BR=4.977 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=2.5 CJC=9.728p MJC=.5776
+ VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=8.063p MJE=.3677 VJE=.75 TR=33.42n TF=179.3p ITF=.4 VTF=4
+ XTF=6 RB=10)

.model DBAT85 D(IS={2.117e-7*ISSCALE} N=1.016 BV=33 IBV=1e-5 RS=2.763
+ CJO=11.5p VJ=0.2 M=0.3 FC=0.5 TT=0 EG=0.69 XTI=2)

* Pet-pin switch: closed = GPIO driving (about 40 ohm), open = high-Z.
.model SWPET SW(VT=0.5 VH=0.1 RON=40 ROFF=1e10)
